    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1255">

                <pb facs="1008" n="892" xml:id="pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.2311/31.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Secretaries of the Treasury, of Commerce and Labor, and
                            of War</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Identic telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This Department’s telegram of the 8th instant. The Governor of Texas has been
                    informed that the Mexican troops in question are to be used for general
                    hostilities in the State of Chihuahua and has accordingly seen fit to withdraw
                    his consent to their passage over Texan territory, and has so informed this
                    Department. I must consequently cancel my request that your Department render
                    assistance in the matter and say instead that I will appreciate it if you will
                    promptly cancel any orders that have already been given and see that nothing
                    further is done.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
